/* ==========================================================================
   United States Universities For Ukraine — i18n.js

   Bilingual engine (English ⇄ Ukrainian). Load this BEFORE main.js.

   How it works
   ------------
   The English text in the HTML is the dictionary key. When the visitor
   switches to Ukrainian, every text node and common attribute on the
   page is looked up in the `uk` map below and swapped if a translation
   exists. Untranslated strings simply stay English — nothing breaks.

   How to add content in both languages
   ------------------------------------
   1. Write the English text in the page as usual.
   2. Add one line here:  "The English text": "Український переклад",
   Keys are whitespace-collapsed, so wrapped lines in HTML still match.
   Note: text split by tags (e.g. <br />) forms separate keys per line.

   Public API (used by main.js and auth.js)
   ----------------------------------------
   USUFU_I18N.lang()   -> "en" | "uk"
   USUFU_I18N.t(text)  -> translated string for dynamic UI
   USUFU_I18N.apply()  -> translate the current document (runs on load)
   ========================================================================== */

